.TH WALLRACK 1 "2026-06-12" "wallrack 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wallrack \- modular, picker-agnostic wallpaper manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wallrack
.I COMMAND
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wallrack
indexes plain image directories and Steam Workshop content (Wallpaper Engine
image scrapes and live WE projects), generates thumbnails, tracks favorites,
tags, and ratings, persists picker state, and applies wallpapers to specific
monitors. Output is structured (JSON or picker script-mode) so any frontend
\(em rofi, fuzzel, walker, wofi, a TUI, a desktop widget \(em can drive it.
.PP
Each command operates on one of three integrations, selected with
.BR \-\-integration :
.TP
.B wallpaper
Plain images from \fBwallpaper.dirs\fR in \fIconfig.toml\fR.
.TP
.B we_image
Images extracted from Wallpaper Engine workshop projects.
.TP
.B we
Live Wallpaper Engine projects, applied via
.BR linux-wallpaperengine .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B index [\-\-integration=\fIWHICH\fB]
Build or refresh the on-disk index and thumbnails.
.I WHICH
is
.BR all " (default), " wallpaper ", " we_image ", or " we .
.TP
.B list [\-\-integration=\fIWHICH\fB] [\-\-format=\fIFMT\fB] [\-\-favorites] [\-\-tag=\fITAG\fB] [\-\-rating=\fIR\fB] [\-\-folder=\fIPATH\fB] [\-\-use-state] [\-\-group]
Emit wallpapers in the requested format. With
.B \-\-use\-state
the filters are pulled from persisted picker state instead of flags.
.B \-\-group
collapses subfolders into folder rows (wallpaper-style integrations only).
.TP
.B view [\-\-format=\fIFMT\fB]
Render the current picker view based on persisted state. This is the entry
point reference frontends (e.g. the bundled rofi script) call on each
invocation.
.TP
.B tags [\-\-integration=\fIWHICH\fB] [\-\-format=\fIFMT\fB]
List the unique tags currently in the active integration's index.
.TP
.B tag \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Edit per-entry tag overrides. Subcommands:
.BR add ", " remove ", " set ", " clear ", " show ", " available ", "
.BR create ", " delete .
.BR delete " accepts " \-\-cascade
to also strip the tag from every entry that carries it.
.TP
.B rating \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Edit per-entry rating overrides. Subcommands:
.BR set ", " clear ", " show .
.TP
.B favorites \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manage favorites. Subcommands:
.BR list ", " add ", " remove ", " toggle ", " is .
.B is
exits 0 if the id is favorited, 1 otherwise.
.B toggle
prints
.RB \(lq added \(rq " or " \(lq removed \(rq.
.TP
.B state \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Picker state get/set/reset. Subcommands:
.BR get ", " set ", " unset ", " dump ", " reset-transient .
.BR reset-transient
clears
.IR drill_path ", " tag_mode ", " tag_edit_target ", " tag_add_mode .
.TP
.B monitors [\-\-integration=\fIWHICH\fB] [\-\-target=\fIID\fB] [\-\-format=\fIFMT\fB]
List monitors with their current wallpapers in the requested format.
.I target
is passed through in the
.B info
field so picker scripts can route the selection back to
.BR apply .
.TP
.B apply [\-\-integration=\fIWHICH\fB] \-\-monitor=\fIMON\fR \fITARGET\fR
Apply
.I TARGET
(image path or WE folder path) to monitor
.IR MON .
Runs
.B hooks.pre_apply_hook
before and
.B hooks.post_apply_hook
after the apply, if configured. Both receive
.BR WALLRACK_WALLPAPER ", " WALLRACK_MONITOR ", " WALLRACK_INTEGRATION
in the environment.
.TP
.B daemon \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Daemon control. Subcommands:
.BR start " [" \-\-foreground "], " stop ", " status .
The daemon watches the configured directories and re-indexes incrementally
when content changes.
.TP
.B info
Show resolved paths, per-integration index sizes, configured wallpaper
directories, and the active hook commands.
.SH OUTPUT FORMATS
.B \-\-format
accepts:
.BR json " (default for machine consumption), "
.BR rofi " (rofi script-mode \(em see " rofi-script (5) ),"
.BR walker ", " wofi ", " fuzzel
(dmenu-style for the respective launchers).
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B wallrack
reads
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wallrack/config.toml
(falling back to
.IR ~/.config/wallrack/config.toml ).
See the bundled
.I config.example.toml
for the full schema, including
.BR wallpaper.dirs ", " workshop_dir ", per-integration backend commands "
.RB ( apply_cmd ", " monitors_cmd ", " current_image_cmd "), and the "
.BR [hooks] " section."
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wallrack/config.toml
User configuration.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/wallrack/
Per-integration index JSON, thumbnails, picker state, favorites, tag
overrides, tag catalog, and rating overrides.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ROFI_RETV
When set,
.B wallrack
assumes it is running inside a rofi script-mode invocation and emits
.BR notify-send (1)
progress notifications during indexing.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Standard
.BR env_logger (3)
filter \(em set to
.BR debug " or " info
for verbose output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success;
.B 1
on
.B favorites is
when the id is not favorited, or on a missing state key for
.BR state get .
Non-zero on any other error, with a diagnostic on stderr.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Build every integration's index:
.PP
.RS
.nf
wallrack index
.fi
.RE
.PP
List the
.B we
integration as JSON for a TUI frontend:
.PP
.RS
.nf
wallrack list \-\-integration=we \-\-format=json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Toggle a favorite from a hotkey:
.PP
.RS
.nf
wallrack favorites toggle \-\-integration=wallpaper /path/to/image.jpg
.fi
.RE
.PP
Apply a wallpaper to a specific monitor:
.PP
.RS
.nf
wallrack apply \-\-integration=wallpaper \-\-monitor=DP\-1 /path/to/image.jpg
.fi
.RE
.PP
Start the watcher daemon in the foreground:
.PP
.RS
.nf
wallrack daemon start \-\-foreground
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rofi-script (5),
.BR notify-send (1),
.BR hyprctl (1)
.PP
Project home:
